## 6. Recover BST: LeetCode 99

### Pattern

A valid BST inorder must be increasing.

Violation:

```java
prev.val > curr.val
```

At the first violation:

```text
first  = prev
second = curr
```

At later violations:

```text
second = curr
```

Finally, swap `first.val` and `second.val`.

```java
class Solution {
    private TreeNode prev;
    private TreeNode first;
    private TreeNode second;

    public void recoverTree(TreeNode root) {
        inorder(root);

        int temp = first.val;
        first.val = second.val;
        second.val = temp;
    }

    private void inorder(TreeNode curr) {
        if (curr == null) {
            return;
        }

        inorder(curr.left);

        if (prev != null && prev.val > curr.val) {
            if (first == null) {
                first = prev;
            }

            second = curr;
        }

        prev = curr;

        inorder(curr.right);
    }
}
```

### Memory shortcut

```text
first is assigned only once.
second is updated whenever a violation occurs.
```

