## 7. LCA in BST: LeetCode 235

### Pattern

```text
Both p and q smaller than root → go left
Both p and q greater than root → go right
Otherwise                     → root is LCA
```

```java
class Solution {
    public TreeNode lowestCommonAncestor(
            TreeNode root,
            TreeNode p,
            TreeNode q) {

        while (root != null) {
            if (p.val < root.val && q.val < root.val) {
                root = root.left;
            } else if (p.val > root.val && q.val > root.val) {
                root = root.right;
            } else {
                return root;
            }
        }

        return null;
    }
}
```

### Why does `else` give the answer?

It means:

```text
p and q are on different sides
OR
one of them is the current root
```

Therefore, the current root is where their paths meet.

